    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0438" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-03T01:00:00+08:00">March 3, 1947—1
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received—3:13 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>424. Following from Taipei:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote"><p>“March 2, 5 p.m. Light firing heard last night and
                        throughout today, while situation remains tense.</p>
                    <p>“In radio speech this afternoon Governor General agreed to people’s demands
                        as enunciated by local PPC<anchor n="10" xml:id="d332-f1"/> member acting as
                        spokesman that all Formosans seized during incident be released
                        unconditionally <pb facs="0439" n="429" xml:id="pg429"/> and that damages or
                        medical treatment be given behalf those killed and wounded. No reference in
                        speech to other demands that Monoply and Trading Bureau systems be
                        abolished.</p>
                    <p>“All Government departments and services inoperative both Taipei-Keelung.
                        Island-wide disturbances reported.”</p></quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Butterworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
